---
// Two answers from the Acme demo: a "not documented" that is flagged, and an answer cited to Notion pages.
---

<section id="chat" class="chat wrap section split">
  <div class="col-text">
    <span class="kicker">// the chatbot</span>
    <h2 class="h2">Cites everything. Says when it does not know.</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      Every fact links to its Notion page. When Notion has no answer, it says so and flags the question for the next
      update. So does a thumbs down.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="col-wide chat-card" role="group" aria-label="Example answers">
    <div class="turn turn-first">
      <div class="question">What is our parental leave top-up policy?</div>
      <div class="gap-note">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#B0003A" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle>
          <path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path>
        </svg>
        <div>
          This is not documented in Notion yet. I searched <b>people</b> and <b>legal</b> for "parental leave" and "top-up".
          Flagged for the next update.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="turn">
      <div class="question">Why can't I enable live chat on a client group?</div>
      <div class="answer">
        A group can only use the channels allowed for its company <span class="cite">[1]</span>. Add live chat to the
        company's allowed channels first, then enable it on the group <span class="cite">[2]</span>.
      </div>
      <div class="sources">[1] Admin &gt; Companies &nbsp; [2] Admin &gt; Groups</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .chat {
    align-items: center;
  }
  .chat-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .turn {
    padding: 22px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .turn-first {
    gap: 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
  }
  .question {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .gap-note {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--accent-deeper);
  }
  .gap-note svg {
    flex: none;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .answer {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .cite {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 2px 6px;
  }
  .sources {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
